REQ-PRODUCTION-001,IMPLEMENTED,558,559,,"PR #559 implements the M4 persistent ProductionUnit state boundary: live installedCapital is the sole mutable capacity stock; ProductionSignalState and lastLifecycleReviewTick are materialized at genesis; INPUT/OUTPUT/INVESTMENT inventories remain distinct physical maps; deriveNameplateCapacity derives batches per tick strictly as installedCapital × RecipeDefinition.batchesPerCapitalUnit without a serialized capacity authority; validateProductionUnitPersistentState rejects non-finite or negative capital/inventory, inventory aliasing, out-of-range or non-finite signals, invalid counters and review ticks; genesis reconciliation reads live installedCapital and its capital-removal negative control mutates the live authority. Focused proof: src/simulation/productionUnitState.test.ts (8 tests) plus the updated genesisReconciliation capital-removal negative control. Exact-head CI run 35306175336 on 260973f5255a7c7c84c6bf226a3366539fd4ae28 passed TypeScript typecheck/tests/build, retained .NET build/test, policy-guard and mergeability. MERGE_COMMIT intentionally blank until integration; no Phase-2 planning, production execution, investment execution, lifecycle transition behavior, M5+, or mirror change is claimed."
